<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caracalla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">188–217</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Caracalla was Roman emperor from 198, jointly with his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septimius-severus">Septimius Severus</a> and then his brother Geta, and sole ruler from 211 to 217 after having Geta murdered. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutio-antoniniana">Constitutio Antoniniana</a> of 212 granted Roman citizenship to almost all free inhabitants of the empire, and he built the great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bath">Baths</a> of Caracalla in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. He was assassinated near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-carrhae">Carrhae</a> while campaigning against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthia">Parthia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caracalla.jpg" alt="Caracalla" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Pol GRANDMONT · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:0_Caracalla_-_Museo_Massimo_alle_Terme.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
